		<script>
			var _commentsData = {"settings":{"i":{"approveComments":true,"bootstrapTime":"2017-04-29T14:51:35.710Z","emailNotification":"_notify","enableEmoji":true,"enableImageAttachments":true,"enableNewCompose":true,"enableRating":true,"enableReplyNotification":true,"enableVotes":true,"enableWebsite":true,"exp":{"freeNotifications":true},"hideSocial":false,"optionalEmailBox":true,"replies":"users","showSocialSharing":true,"version":1},"w":{"bootstrapTime":1532811801823,"comment":{"background":"$color-8","textColor":"$color-1","textColorInherit":true,"transparentBackground":true},"commentsPerPage":10,"count":{"messages":9},"enableVK":false,"lang":"en","settingsOpened":true,"version":9,"widget":{"background":"$color-1","border":{"color":"$color-6","round":true,"show":false,"width":1},"buttonColor":"$color-8","fontSize":14,"textColor":"$color-5","titleSize":24,"transparentBackground":false}}},"comments":{"-M2-p_VpulMtoBTQPbLg":{"author":"Sandra Roberts","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"I tried this recipe and it turned out nothing like described and pictured. They were like hard tack. I don't know what happened and was very disappointed after working on them most of the day.","thread":{"-M6_4d12U7i9POoWxTo0":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Hello Sandra, I'm so sorry you had a bad experience with these. There are many things that can effect the rising of any bread or roll that can result in a very hard dense texture. Most often the problem is with the yeast or starter not being active enough. The starter should be fed the night before or the morning of baking and have at least some bubbly activity and it's a good idea to check the expiration date on the dry yeast. Also be sure that the warm liquid used in the recipe is not hotter than 108 degrees. My daughter once used the water from our hot water tap and killed the yeast immediately. Needless to say, those rolls turned out exactly as you describe. I hope you will try again :0) Please let me know if I can answer any more questions for you.","time":1588686393602,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"}},"time":1583783255509,"userId":"d48e5547d643cea4656477f82cfde54b","userType":"email"},"-M6LS17udL0LRQL7Glpa":{"author":"Holly","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"directions call for water but not listed in the ingredients? And doesn’t say when to add milk? \n","thread":{"-M6LiyuMHndgs83OAkgA":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","text":"Hi Holly! Thanks for pointing this out to me. You should use 1 cup + a few tablespoons if needed, of either Milk, water or whey. They can be used interchangeably in this recipe depending on what you have on hand. If you use milk or whey you will be making a more enriched bread, higher in protein and such, than if you use water. I hope I've corrected the wording in this post so it's less confusing and I hope you give the recipe a try. Please let me know if you have any other questions. Stay healthy!❤\n\n","time":1588445240947,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"},"-M6VpYm1sTayo7nWA4Z_":{"author":"Holly ","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","text":"I have made these 3 times. They’re easy and delicious! It’s a keeper. I used milk ","time":1588615069712,"userId":"visitor","userType":"anonymous"}},"time":1588440868390,"userId":"f0c4ba40173ecd63a78d9b3ef131417c","userType":"email"},"-M6ZrVSdhqNUMLJvO9Ao":{"author":"sonal","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"is it possible to skip the active dry yeast entirely and use only the starter? ","thread":{"-M6_2ambLp07hUWt4fBi":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"It is possible to leave out the dry yeast. If you choose to go without it, the rising times will be significantly longer. Be sure to use very active sourdough starter as well. Freshly fed and very bubbly for best results. Please let me know if you try it that way and how it worked out for you :0)","time":1588685860135,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"}},"time":1588682688368,"userId":"dd202e7769b8581278a391d12635868e","userType":"email"},"-M6eg3G4uAeqb0MUdj0h":{"attachment":"$attach:a888475b-6c6a-476f-9e36-6251306ee0d0\/048dbf5738a431231425b53b34d6e520.jpg","author":"Sonal","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"They turned out delicious with just the starter and no yeast! \nIt's very very warm right now in Mumbai so the rising happens quickly. \n❤","thread":{"-M6ejRhhgtEDc0s6n5dH":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"I'm so glad to hear they turned out well! Having very warm weather is so helpful when rising. Cheers! :0)","time":1588781239214,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"}},"time":1588780355719,"userId":"visitor","userType":"anonymous","voteData":{"b2e5108fb1b09b0f0d8073f2b5279bbb6d36be35fc666d3f96c95517c842231e":1,"fb66e00c33e942be62d02b494d2d7c0d63fd073488401221c94cf8346e7ebea7":1},"votes":2},"-MMfevj1Rfe5WWwIWU_F":{"author":"Deanna","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Have you tried to freeze these? I want to make the, in advance, would I freeze the dough or the baked rolls?\n","thread":{"-MMflWXz6TfVoJ1zxicN":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Absolutely! Bake them and freeze them. I've done this many times. Sometimes I under bake them just a touch so they don't overbrown when re-heating. If you wrap them in foil that won't be a problem. I like to thaw them completely before re-heating but I'm sure that's not really necessary. I'd love to know how yours turn out!","time":1605978429718,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"}},"time":1605976702215,"userId":"5237c7396e167d3286dfafc5d8dd8cc2","userType":"email"},"-MMvYR8Gq4RqRo4sbWcJ":{"author":"Deanna","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Mine sadly turned out more \nIke delicious biscuits than rolls. I used a candy thermometer to be sure my milk was the perfect temperature so I know o didn’t kill the yeast. Delicious, but not a fluffy roll I was hoping for. \n","thread":{"-MMvkl6Ro6_tsROmbQ6I":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","text":"Hi Deanna, I'm so sorry they didn't turn out the way you expected. That doesn't sound like it went quite right for you. How long did they proof (rise) the first time and did the dough rise well for you? Once you made them into rolls, did they rise again? I'm glad the flavor is good!\n","time":1606246210342,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"},"-MMwFZwLES8z3DtKj-UI":{"author":"Deanna ","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","text":"I let it rise 90 minutes, it was doubled, I then made into rounds and let rise again. The dough felt more like sourdough bread dough, not fluffy like I expected with the extra yeast. ","time":1606255005916,"userId":"5237c7396e167d3286dfafc5d8dd8cc2","userType":"email"},"-MMwR2BG9sO4BvH78bx9":{"author":"Melisa","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","text":"Butter is really a key factor to make them a softer roll. Butter in the dough and on the top while they are still warm. Also, all sourdough softens after being placed in a plastic bag overnight or covered in plastic wrap in the baking pan. If you put them under wraps in the fridge they may be more what you expect tomorrow.  \n\n","time":1606258012802,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userType":"email"}},"time":1606243173364,"userId":"5237c7396e167d3286dfafc5d8dd8cc2","userType":"email"},"-MS0VU_RXFjbgia37wX1":{"author":"Rhonda","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Thinking about making these but I only have unbleached flour at home. Could I use 3 cups of that? Thank you for your help. ","thread":{"-MS12JQ0mhb6Ix9-NOuR":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Yes absolutely! Please let me know how they turn out for you. :0)","time":1611720902883,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"}},"time":1611711775057,"userId":"visitor","userType":"anonymous"},"-MZnUWXwUwUWTugLuE4c":{"author":"Patty ","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Could you use low fat drinkable yogurt in this recipe?","thread":{"-MZrgnR35_K0WeRGg-JS":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"I'm sure you could use low fat drinkable yogurt in place of the water, whey or milk I've used for these sourdough pull apart rolls. Never tried it but sounds delicious!","time":1620137162567,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"},"-MZxoaMqBLyMQSeTw3aK":{"author":"Patty ","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","text":"Very good flavor with the yogurt. I will need to make them again to get the rise rite.","time":1620239866907,"userId":"189cecc4a7a7ddb9b7c20ad248f2af72","userType":"email"}},"time":1620066571967,"userId":"189cecc4a7a7ddb9b7c20ad248f2af72","userType":"email"},"-MmZ2w-x9jyg2DOXjtIo":{"author":"Lisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Could I get your sourdough starter recipe😁\n\n","thread":{"-MmcrhlRBH_zuEMOj0nF":{"author":"Melisa","page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Thanks for your request! It reminded me to add a link to my recipe for the starter and a few others, including the care and keeping of sourdough starter. I hope you enjoy them! They are now on this webpage just above the recipe for the sourdough pull-apart rolls.","time":1634920750238,"userId":"9acc1803bb49d8e1f565ad16cecad0ab","userPic":"$profile:7ab789456869965485e7389825cfb8d0.jpg","userType":"email"}},"time":1634840069430,"userId":"visitor","userType":"anonymous"},"-Oa2YIyacmU2Iv4jv22r":{"author":"Pat","notifications":true,"page":"http:\/\/www.theglasspantry.com\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","pageTitle":"Sourdough Pull-Apart Rolls","path":"\/sourdough-pull-apart-rolls","text":"Can this dough be used for cinnamon rolls ","time":1758848696653,"userId":"628744a1e28aa357714290374072f347","userType":"email"}},"texts":null};
